title: Exact ERC-20 transfers and readable reverts in the assets and asset-conversion precompiles

doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    Since #13230, a `pallet-assets` transfer that would leave the source a remainder below the
    asset's `min_balance` sweeps that remainder to the destination and reports the whole amount.
    ERC-20 requires `transfer(to, value)` and `transferFrom(from, to, value)` to move exactly
    `value`, so the assets ERC-20 precompile now refuses such a transfer instead. Before
    `do_transfer` / `do_transfer_approved` it calls `fungibles::Inspect::can_withdraw` and
    reverts with "Transfer would leave sender below minimum balance" when that returns
    `ReducedToZero` with a non-zero remainder. Sending the whole balance and self-transfers are
    unaffected. `pallet-assets` itself is unchanged. XCM reaches this path through
    `ERC20Transactor` when it names a precompile address, so such an XCM now fails instead of
    moving more than it declared.

    Both precompiles now revert, with the reason sp-runtime gives a `DispatchError`, for every
    pallet failure of a state-changing call. Module errors carry their variant name (for example
    "AssetNotLive", "BalanceLow", "PoolEmpty"), so a contract sees the same name whichever
    precompile surfaced it. These used to trap with empty return data. `Error::Error` remains
    for charging failures, and for a state change under `STATICCALL`, which fails with no return
    data as it does on Ethereum and elsewhere in revive.

    The asset-conversion precompile keeps a few deliberate reasons. `getReserves` and the quote
    calls tell a missing pool ("Pool does not exist") from one without liquidity ("Pool exists
    but has no liquidity"), which reads `AssetConversion::Pools`; `pallet-asset-conversion`
    gains `Pallet::pool_exists` and a `WeightInfo::pool_exists` benchmark, charged only when the
    reserves come back empty. A zero quote amount reverts with "Amount can't be zero", and any
    other failed quote with "Quote failed". A swap whose withdrawal would not be exact reverts
    with "Swap amount cannot be withdrawn exactly".

    `pallet_asset_conversion`'s `withdraw` helper now refuses a credit that differs from the
    requested value. An expendable `pallet-assets` withdrawal could sweep a remainder into the
    credit, which was then paid into the pool while the swap was priced on the requested amount.
    Every path into `withdraw` is transactional, so the refused withdrawal is rolled back. Native
    withdrawals are exact and unaffected.

    The `pallet_revive::Error::PrecompileDelegateDenied` doc no longer claims the calling
    contract is trapped.

- audience: Runtime User
  description: |-
    ERC-20 `transfer` and `transferFrom` on `pallet-assets` tokens now revert with "Transfer
    would leave sender below minimum balance" instead of moving more than `value` when the
    sender would be left holding less than the asset's minimum balance. Send the whole balance,
    or leave at least the minimum. The same applies to XCM that moves such a token through its
    precompile address.

    Contracts calling the assets ERC-20 or the asset-conversion precompile can now catch
    `Error(string)` for pallet failures. Reasons are error variant names such as
    "AssetNotLive", "BalanceLow", "Unapproved" or "PoolEmpty". A `DELEGATECALL` reverts with
    "illegal to call this pre-compile via delegate call". A state-changing call under
    `STATICCALL` still fails with empty return data.

    Asset-conversion quotes no longer share "Pool does not exist or has no liquidity". They
    report "Amount can't be zero", "Pool does not exist", "Pool exists but has no liquidity", or
    "Quote failed"; `getReserves` reports the same pool reasons. Update any caller that matched
    the old string or the old empty return data.

crates:
# `WeightInfo` gains `pool_exists`, which every implementor must add.
- name: pallet-asset-conversion
  bump: major
- name: pallet-assets-precompiles
  bump: patch
- name: pallet-asset-conversion-precompiles
  bump: patch
# Doc comment only.
- name: pallet-revive
  bump: none
# Implement the new `pallet_asset_conversion::WeightInfo::pool_exists`.
- name: asset-hub-westend-runtime
  bump: patch
- name: asset-hub-rococo-runtime
  bump: patch
- name: pallet-staking-async-parachain-runtime
  bump: patch
